# Layer 2 — Full Document: WFI-008 Skill Definition Standard
# Retrieved on demand via get_canon_doc("WFI-008")

@doc WFI-008 [std, active, agents+employees] v2 sha:7d4a1f
@links WFI-001,WFI-002,WFI-003,WFI-009
@cycle 90d
@reviewed 2026-04-14

@vocab
  depends_on    | skill cannot be effectively applied without target present
  adjacent_to   | skills frequently co-occur and complement; symmetric
  progression_to | target represents natural advancement from source

@def skill
  Atomic, distinct, demonstrable capability enabling effective task performance.
  Learned through education, training, or experience. Observable through behavior,
  outcomes, or artifacts. Identity stable across industries and tools.

@props
  + atomicity        | single bounded unit, not a bundle
  + distinctness     | clear identity boundary, no semantic overlap
  + observability    | demonstrable through performance or outputs
  + trainability     | developable through learning or practice
  + outcome-rel      | contributes to measurable work outcomes
  + ctx-independence | identity stable across contexts
  + prof-measurable  | evaluable at differing mastery levels
  + canon-resolvable | alternate terms resolve to single canonical ID

@include
  ? single bounded capability
  ? demonstrable through execution or outcomes
  ? intentionally developable
  ? stable meaning independent of employer or tool
  ? distinguishable from adjacent skills with clear scope boundary

@exclude
  ! role, task, job title
  ! tool, software, hardware, platform
  ! broad capability bundle
  ! personality trait or attitude alone
  ! process step or workflow state
  ! customer label without distinct canonical capability

@constraints
  skill
  mutex: lifecycleStatus=Active AND lifecycleStatus=Deprecated
  requires: AIImpactCategory IS SET when AiWorkforceReductionPercent > 0
  forbids: depends_on cycle-length > 3
  enforced-by: ontology-rule-layer

@rel
  depends_on    -> Skill [conf:high]
  adjacent_to   <=> Skill [conf:medium]
  progression_to -> Skill [conf:high]
  requires      <- Role [weight:critical]
  requires      <- Task
  develops      <- Program
  demonstrates  <- Individual
  demonstrates  <- Agent

@attrs required
  id                    | canonical skill identifier
  title                 | canonical display name
  description           | definition text
  lifecycleStatus       | active | inactive | draft | deprecated
  version               | semantic version
  taxonomy/category     | single home in the two-level taxonomy
  atomicity-validation  | pass | fail | pending
  scope-boundary-notes  | free text clarifying identity edges

@attrs optional
  skillType              | technical | interpersonal | cognitive | physical
  AIImpactCategory       | Automated | Augmented | Amplified | Stable
  AIImpactRating         | high | medium | low
  AIImpactMechanism      | free text
  delegationLevel        | full | supervised | not-delegable
  transferabilityScore   | 0.0–1.0
  collaborationIntensity | high | medium | low
  scarcityLevel          | scarce | available | surplus
  proficiencyIndicators  | free text
  assessmentMethods      | free text

@disallowed
  ! bundled phrases combining multiple capabilities
  ! titles describing workflow state not capability
  ! synonyms treated as new canonical skills
  ! tool names unless capability is distinct from tool familiarity
